; Root environment: variables shared across packages, plus the root scripts, migrations and tests.
;
; Package-only settings live in that package's template: backend ones (Auth0 M2M, Cloudinary,
; Hive, Anthropic, Google Drive, OpenTelemetry, log levels, …) in packages/server/.env.template,
; client ones (AUTH0_FRONTEND_CLIENT_ID, GRAPHQL_URL, DEV_AUTH_USER_ID) in
; packages/client/.env.template, bank-scraper dev credentials in
; packages/modern-poalim-scraper/.env.template, and so on.
;
; Several packages fall back to this file for anything their own .env does not set, so whatever
; is set here reaches them too: the server, the client, the modern-poalim-scraper dev scripts,
; israeli-vat-scraper (its USER_CODE included) and the green-invoice-graphql dev e2e script.
; mcp-server, the email-ingestion gateway and the crypto scrapers read only their own .env.
;
; Conventions: active entries are required for local development; commented-out `# VAR=value`
; entries are optional. `scripts/__tests__/env-templates.test.ts` fails on an entry nothing reads.

############
# Database #
############

; LOCAL DATABASE ONLY. The root .env must never hold credentials for production, or for any
; other deployed database.
;
; This file is read by codegen, migrations, seeds and every DB-backed test, so whatever is set
; here is what `yarn test`, `yarn generate` and `migration:run` all target -- including
; `vitest --project unit`, whose global setup writes reference data before any test runs.
;
; Credentials for a deployed database belong in a separate, explicitly named file (e.g.
; .env.production, also git-ignored) that you pass deliberately, to one command -- never here.
;
; The checks below are a second line of defence, not a reason to relax that rule, and they
; are not uniform (packages/migrations/src/local-db-guard.ts, scripts/demo-seed-guard.ts):
;   - DB-backed tests, the vitest global setup and `yarn seed:production` REFUSE a non-local
;     host, unless you opt in for that one command with ALLOW_REMOTE_DB=1
;   - the demo seed test (`yarn test:demo-seed`) REFUSES a non-local host; nothing overrides it
;   - the demo seed (`yarn seed:staging-demo`) truncates the domain tables, so it REFUSES a
;     non-local host without ALLOW_REMOTE_DB=1, and on any host it REFUSES a database whose
;     name says production, whatever is set. Otherwise it runs only for a demo database, local
;     or remote (see ALLOW_DEMO_SEED_DATABASE below)
;   - `migration:run` only WARNS and then proceeds, because production deploys may apply
;     migrations during the build; set ENFORCE_LOCAL_DB=1 to make it refuse too
;   - codegen (`yarn generate` / pgTyped) is NOT guarded at all -- it only reads, so it will
;     silently introspect whatever host is set here
;
; Shared with the server. `1` connects over SSL (default: 0).
POSTGRES_USER=postgres
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres
POSTGRES_HOST=localhost
POSTGRES_PORT=5432
POSTGRES_DB=accounter
POSTGRES_SSL='0'

; Schema the DB-backed tests and `scripts/verify-migrations.ts` inspect (default: accounter_schema).
# POSTGRES_SCHEMA=accounter_schema

; Recommended on every developer machine. `1` makes `migration:run`, the one command that
; otherwise only warns about a non-local host, refuse it instead. Deploys leave it unset, which
; is why refusing is not the default. Prefer `export ENFORCE_LOCAL_DB=1` in your shell profile
; (~/.zshrc, ~/.bashrc) over uncommenting it here: the profile also covers checkouts and git
; worktrees that have no .env of their own.
# ENFORCE_LOCAL_DB=1

; Per-command opt-in: `ALLOW_REMOTE_DB=1 <command>` lets the DB-backed tests, the seeds and
; (under ENFORCE_LOCAL_DB=1) `migration:run` target a non-local host for that one command. It
; does not unlock the demo seed test, and for the demo seed it is not enough by itself: the
; database also has to be a demo database (below). Never set it in this file or in a shell
; profile: tests and seeds refuse to run if it is in this file.
# ALLOW_REMOTE_DB=1

#########
# Seeds #
#########

; `yarn seed:production` (scripts/seed.ts): accounts to create for the admin business. Add more
; with a numeric suffix (SEED_BANK_ACCOUNT_NUMBER_2, SEED_BANK_NUMBER_2, SEED_BRANCH_NUMBER_2,
; SEED_CREDIT_CARD_LAST4DIGITS_2, …); the first missing one ends the list.
# SEED_BANK_ACCOUNT_NUMBER=1234567890
# SEED_BANK_NUMBER=12
# SEED_BRANCH_NUMBER=123
# SEED_CREDIT_CARD_LAST4DIGITS=1234
; Comma-separated currencies: each seeded account gets a tax category per currency.
# SEED_CURRENCIES=USD,ILS

; Demo seed (`yarn seed:staging-demo`, scripts/seed-demo-data.ts). It TRUNCATEs every domain table.
; Per-command opt-in: the script refuses to run without `ALLOW_DEMO_SEED=1`, with
; NODE_ENV=production, or against a non-local host without `ALLOW_REMOTE_DB=1`. `yarn
; test:demo-seed` needs it on the command too: the test is skipped without it and never sets
; it. Never set it in this file: tests and seeds refuse to run if it is.
# ALLOW_DEMO_SEED=1
; Which databases the demo seed accepts (scripts/demo-seed-guard.ts): one whose name carries
; staging, stage, demo, test, testing, preview, sandbox, e2e or local; the dev container's
; `accounter`, on a local host only; and never, on any host, one whose name carries prod,
; production, prd or live. Any other database, a local copy of production included, has to be
; confirmed by name: the value must equal its database name exactly. Put it on the command (for
; a deploy, in the build command), never in this file: tests and seeds refuse to run if it is.
# ALLOW_DEMO_SEED_DATABASE=accounter_uat
; Optional Auth0 user id to link to the seeded demo admin user. Leave unset to seed it without an
; Auth0 identity.
# DEMO_AUTH0_USER_ID=

########
# Auth #
########

; Auth0 tenant domain (bare hostname) and API audience. Shared: the server verifies tokens with
; them and the client requests tokens for them.
AUTH0_DOMAIN=your-tenant.us.auth0.com
AUTH0_AUDIENCE=https://api.accounter.com

; Local development only: `1` lets the client send, and the server accept, an
; `X-Dev-Auth: <user-id>` header instead of an Auth0 login. Must be `1` or `0` (the server refuses
; to start otherwise). Never set in a deployed environment. Pick the user with DEV_AUTH_USER_ID
; (see packages/client/.env.template).
# ALLOW_DEV_AUTH=1

#######################
# Tooling and runtime #
#######################

; `yarn migration:check-conflicts` (scripts/check-migration-conflicts.ts). `1` only warns on
; conflicts, `0` (the default) fails. The refs default to origin/main and HEAD.
# MIGRATION_CONFLICT_WARN_ONLY=0
# MIGRATION_CONFLICT_BASE_REF=origin/main
# MIGRATION_CONFLICT_HEAD_REF=HEAD

; Local development only (richer library logs). Never set in production: libraries key their debug
; output off DEBUG, and some of it includes request headers and bodies. Server and Green Invoice
; logs ignore it; use SERVER_LOG_LEVEL and GREEN_INVOICE_LOG_LEVEL (see packages/server/.env.template).
; `DEBUG=accounter:test` turns on the server test-harness diagnostics.
DEBUG=1

; Leave unset locally. Every package that falls back to this file inherits it: `production` makes
; the demo seed refuse to run and switches the server to production behaviour (masked errors,
; OTEL_DEPLOYMENT_ENV). Deployed environments set it themselves.
# NODE_ENV=development

; Any non-empty value silences dotenv's debug output in the server and in migrations (which, when it
; is unset, also loads packages/migrations/.env). Meant for deployed environments.
# RELEASE=1
